# ---------------- section 8.8 ----------------
("""- **The owner sometimes edits `doc/` himself** (`6de0d99` removed the direction v0.2 copy): report what you see, never touch `doc/`, and fold the change into the next document package.""",
"""- **The owner sometimes edits `doc/` himself** (`6de0d99` removed the direction v0.2 copy): report what you see, never touch `doc/`, and fold the change into the next document package.
- **The deny list matches command text** (`*.bat*`, `*results_master*`, `*lottery*`, `*unlink*`, `*rmtree*`, `git -C *`, `git add*`, `git rm*`, and since F1 `*process_check*`, `*install_records*`, `*Run_Evaluation*`, `*Method_Mode_H*`, `*mode_h*`): denied paths go in plan files; Git in a clone goes through `cc_clone.py git`; check every task file (v1r10 delta, T023).
- **Counted edits only** (assert an anchor occurs exactly once). Diffs between candidates exclude removed files on both sides.
- **Mutation honesty:** "no test plants it" is non-detection, not equivalence; print each equivalent's reason. Token economy: new mutants alone with `--only`, then one final chain; after a one-line change rerun only the changed module and say so.
- **An invalid record is a refusal** (`ModeHRefused`), never an escaping `ValueError`. Oz Lotto's ledger never stores supplementaries.
- **When the reviewer checks your documents, expect real catches** (TAKEOVER-C01 reversed A1's order). State A1's order exactly: read once, compute, publish whole and create-only, validate the published ledger, then `SCORE_COMPLETE`.
- **Hashes:** Git stores these markdown files LF; the owner's checkout is CRLF, and `certutil` there sees CRLF bytes; A1 and the EX messages are stored CRLF. Always say which bytes a hash identifies, and give the owner the CRLF value when he checks a working file.
- **History rewrites:** rehearse on a fresh `--mirror`; limit `--refs` to the affected range; prove tree identity and reachability; pinned `--force-with-lease`; `reset --soft` locally; a bundle holds reachable history only (6 November 2026).
- **The owner commits often outside the reviewed line** (GAIS, `.gitignore`, root `.bat` files, his own handover notes): always `git fetch` and look at what changed outside `exchange/` before building on `main`, and check `.gitignore` and the root files every time.
- **Run the whole suite after the release step too, not only at step 10** (13 November 2026): eight tests failed on the installed `main` because two test modules copied the repository's live install records and assumed the state before the install; every isolated rehearsal had run the suite only before the records existed. Future isolated rehearsals run it again in the post-release state (the owner's decision), never as a new step of the live procedure.
- **Check a record number against the newest register before using it** (register v0.27 reused RAT-28; v0.28 corrected it). The same for EX numbers: check the highest committed one.
- **A rule you remember is still checked against the code** (readiness cold read, 13 November 2026): the updater's first update was believed to be all-or-nothing until the code's order (grab, backup, master, ledger) showed a crash can leave the master replaced without its ledger row (EX_167 B02); and a blank-page browser start was proposed as enough until the reviewer asked for the installed fetcher and parser to meet the real page before any irreversible step (B01).
- **A tool's own advice is not an approval** (R-018 (a)): the updater's "rerun with a wider --months-back" is a reviewed, owner-approved step, never an automatic one.
- **Dress-rehearse an irreversible run on invented data with the installed code and the full cohort** before the owner's first real run (Mode H: about one minute per batch and one per score per game on Linux; `modeh_dress_rehearsal.py`). It found nothing wrong, and it fixed the expected timings and outputs for the readiness sheet."""),
